worker_module_budget
  module "formal_ai_worker_shell_compose.js"
  ceiling 464
  rationale "Browser twin of the issue #1177 shell-command composer. Mirrors `handle_shell_command_compose` in rust/src/solver_handlers/shell_command_compose.rs: action-verb and file-context cues come from data/seed/code-task-cues.lino, and every emitted flag is explained from the manual-page table in data/seed/manual-pages.lino. JavaScript-first twin of native handler keys (shell_command_compose), added under R997-R999 (2026-10-06); growth is the ported handler, not silent regrowth. R1017 (2026-10-07) +3: the composer steps aside when the text-manipulation handler reads a seeded text operation over an inline payload, twin of the Rust `names_text_operation` guard. Ceiling 408 (R1017): a relative path such as data/meta is the search root, mirroring root_path. Ceiling 464 (R1017, 2026-10-07) +56: every request word the composer read from inline arrays now comes from the seeded `shell_cue` role map (shellComposeRoleWords / shellComposeWordAfterLead), an \"ending in .ext\" suffix lead names the -name pattern, and a seeded counting cue pipes a find into `wc -l` explained from the wc manual record (shellComposeCounted / shellComposeFlagLines), twins of Rust role_words / word_after_lead / counted / flag_lines; a seeded `program_artifact` word (a requested function or program) makes the composer step aside for program synthesis."
